Moving down (vy > 0) hits the TOP face, ball is above the brick, push up: `ball.y -= overlapY`. After flip vy < 0, push `-overlapY`. Correct.

Great, the logic works: after flipping, the push direction is opposite to the new velocity direction (i.e., the direction the ball came from).

